## Desk vs portal — the two faces of the UI

- **Desk** (`/app`) is the generated back-office: every DocType automatically
  gets a list view, form view, filters, and reports. This is where agents and
  admins work.
- **Portal / website** pages are public-facing Jinja templates. A file pair
  under `templates/pages/` — `<route>.py` + `<route>.html` — becomes a web
  route automatically. The example:
  `apps/ticketing/ticketing/templates/pages/ticket_stats.{py,html}` serves
  `/ticket_stats`; `get_context()` in the `.py` runs on each request and feeds
  the template.

### Form scripts

`ticket_escalation_rule.js` runs in the browser when the Desk form opens.
`frappe.ui.form.on("Ticket Escalation Rule", { refresh(frm) {…} })` reacts to
form events and individual field changes. Use it for UX guardrails only — the
controller must enforce every rule server-side too (never trust the client).

