## Whitelisted methods and the REST API

Any function decorated with `@frappe.whitelist()` becomes an RPC endpoint at
`/api/method/<dotted.path>`. The example, `apps/ticketing/ticketing/api.py`:

```
GET /api/method/ticketing.api.ticket_stats
```

Frappe also exposes a generated **resource API** for every DocType:

```
GET  /api/resource/Ticket Escalation Rule          # list (respects permissions)
GET  /api/resource/Ticket Escalation Rule/<name>   # read one
POST /api/resource/Ticket Escalation Rule          # create
```

Both APIs honour the session (or token) of the caller and the DocType
permission matrix. Never add `allow_guest=True` to a whitelisted method unless
the data is truly public — lint rule **PY001** flags it.

