## What Frappe Helpdesk adds

**Frappe Helpdesk** is itself just a Frappe app (`helpdesk`, installed by
`docker/init.sh`) — a useful reminder that everything above scales to real
products. It brings:

- The agent UI at `/helpdesk` (a Vue single-page app served by Frappe).
- A family of DocTypes — **`HD Ticket`** (the ticket itself), `HD Team`,
  `HD Agent`, `HD Service Level Agreement`, and more. Browse them in Desk:
  they are ordinary DocTypes with schemas, controllers and permissions.
- REST/RPC endpoints for all of the above, like any DocType.

The `ticketing` app treats Helpdesk as a peer: it listens to `HD Ticket`
events (`doc_events`), queries it from tasks and APIs
(`frappe.get_all("HD Ticket", …)`) and augments it with its own
`Ticket Escalation Rule` DocType — all without touching Helpdesk's code.
{{/if}}

